@@ -359,7 +359,7 @@ Note: New panels added or modified mostly not mentioned here for concision. See
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5528+) Minor **beautified** the [CvCustomizableDomesticAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvCustomizableDomesticAdvisor.py): increase **legend culture text width** so it is not cramped when upscaled. Note: although it is functional, the Custom Domestic Advisor is **not supported** in AdvCiv-SAS as of now, so it is lacking the Finance Tab. See also [KI#123](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#123---fixed-bug-domesticmilitary-advisor-variant-toggles-required-restarting-civ4).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5522+) New **Policy Advisor**. **Beautified**: enlarge **top panels text** so **long civic names don't overflow**. **Remove multiline nationality** information which was **uninfomative** and **crowded vertically** in the **Religions tab** and the **Corporations tab**; use more precise and compact `Leader (ID)` and `HQ (ID)` **one-liner instead** (**ID** also handles **one leader name being used by several players**); **increase row spacing** (now **unified** (was crowded)). **Remove multiline wrapped bonuses** splitting logic in the **Corporations tab**: use one natural comma-separated line (bonuses row height reduced/standardized) since there is enough space after expanding the Policy Advisor and it is more readable. Also add **new rows** (**Bonuses Generated**, **Yields Generated**), and add **first column descriptions** for rows (as of now `Built By:`, `Consumes:`, `Generates:`, `Generates 2:`). Add a **Great Person icon** in `Built By:` row. Change in [CvPolicyAdvisorScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvPolicyAdvisorScreen.py).
 - **Foreign Advisor**: refined its tabs so they can display **up to 12 players**. Notably renamed the Active tab to **Treaties** tab (no longer shows redundant bonuses (since their deal can be cancelled from the bonuses tab)), and **beautified** it with **icons**. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5516+) Always use the unified **table-style info layout** (`drawInfoImproved`) for the Info Tab for stable column behavior: the old hardcoded text spacing (`drawInfoOriginal`) did not **scale with upscaled font text** nor **adjust depending on advisor screen size**. Plus the improved layout has additional **information** like general or specific **colored leader attitude text** related to civic/religion choices (e.g., `[-2]` or `[+1]`). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5518+) **Beautified** the **Espionage Tab** similarly; notably **removed redundant Espionage slider** now that commerce sliders are on the right side of main interface in map view, and **improved text spacing** that **was colliding or overflowing** beyond its panel, and **moved + - buttons under the leader icon** where there is more room and it is more intuitive and easier to click it. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5793+) Show **gold per turn** in **Bonuses Tab** even when **not connected to trade network** (if gold trading is available): previously this was hidden, and would require tediously opening the diplomacy screen of each player, and this is now also consistent with flat gold being shown in techs tab for all players (if gold trading is available). See [KI#132](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#132---enhanced-base-advciv-issue-of-not-showing-rival-gold-per-turn-on-foreign-trade-advisor-bonuses-tab-when-not-connected-to-their-trade-network).
-- Added **"Willing to become vassal"** and **"Vassal"** **icons** in the Foreign Advisor's Glance tab in the human player's row, to help avoid the need to tediously check these up through other screens, in [CvForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignAdvisor.py), and in [CvDLLWidgetData.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDLLWidgetData.cpp) for the corresponding **tooltip** (on hover). See ["Willing to become a vassal" and "vassal" icons](/README.md#willing-to-become-a-vassal-and-vassal-icons-in-foreign-advisors-glance-tab). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5808+) **Split Glance Tab** into **several pages of as of now 16 players** (e.g., 3 pages at SAS48 Worldsize), with clickable left and right arrows for navigation. Fixes **issue of Glance Tab clipping horizontally** if more than 24 players are known and columns being too tight. Last page visited is **remembered and resumed from** on Glance Tab next opening. See [KI#134](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#134---fixed-base-advciv-issue-foreign-diplomacy-advisor-glance-tab-column-icons-overflow-horizontally-with-24-rival-players).
+- Added **"Willing to become vassal"** and **"Vassal"** **icons** in the Foreign Advisor's Glance tab in the human player's row, to help avoid the need to tediously check these up through other screens, in [CvForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignAdvisor.py), and in [CvDLLWidgetData.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDLLWidgetData.cpp) for the corresponding **tooltip** (on hover). See ["Willing to become a vassal" and "vassal" icons](/README.md#willing-to-become-a-vassal-and-vassal-icons-in-foreign-advisors-glance-tab). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5808+) Cap **maximum number of players per page** in the **Glance Tab** (e.g., max 16 players per page gives 3 pages at SAS48 Worldsize (if all players are known)), with **clickable left and right arrows for navigation**. Fixes **issue of Glance Tab clipping horizontally** if more than 24 players are known and columns being too tight. Last page visited is **remembered and resumed from** on Glance Tab next opening. See [KI#134](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#134---fixed-base-advciv-issue-foreign-diplomacy-advisor-glance-tab-column-icons-overflow-horizontally-with-24-rival-players).
 - Reworked the **Military Advisor** in [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py) now with Unit Combat and Units **icons**. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5530+) Note: **unit icon size** is **increased** at **higher resolutions** (e.g., from 24 to 32 if resolution height >= 1440), and **promotion icon size** is **increased** (no longer DLL-hardcoded (was 16)). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5777+) **Lift up the unit panel to full height** (reduces the need for scrolling vertically) and **expand it laterally** to **accomodate lengthy unit rows** (e.g., avoid line wrap if unit name is long, if there are many promotions). Make **show/hide individual unit text clickable** too (more accessible than the small +/- button alone). **Increase leader icon bar from 1 to multiple rows**, and **do not reduce icon size until all rows are full**. For example, at 1080p, 5 rows allow to show up to 45 players (including barbarian) at full leader icon size before leader icon size is reduced. **Reduce Leader icon size reduction** when all rows are full (**mild reduction**, no longer halved). See also [KI#123](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#123---fixed-bug-domesticmilitary-advisor-variant-toggles-required-restarting-civ4), [KI#130](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#130---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-unit-rows-showing-build-player-name-instead-of-improvement-text-military-advisor-map-tab), and [KI#131](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#131---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-live-unit-build-action-text-not-being-space-separated-from-its-turn-timer). Note 2: as of now the [CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py) is not supported.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5771+) Added a new **Battles tab** in the Military Advisor, showing as a **sortable table** the detailed **record of each battle** for the selected player in debug dropdown (or the active player or its vassals outside debug mode): **Turn**, **Year**, **Result** (Won, Lost, Retreat) as emoji, **Estimated Odds %** (simple starting effective strength comparison, not exact Civ4 combat odds), **Role** (Are we the attacker?) as emoji, **base Strength** (XML), **start effective Strength** (including modifiers at that battle), **end effective Strength**, **max effective Strength**, **XP before combat** (yellow if Great-General-led), **Our Unit**, **Their Unit** (unit name in yellow if Great-General-led), **same** strength/XP columns for their unit, **Civ icon**, **Player icon**, **Player ID** (to cover the same leader picked by several leaders (custom games, etc.)), **Captured Unit type**, **Captured Unit icon**, **Hill or Peak icon**, **Terrain icon**, **Feature icon**, **Click Plot icon** (**on click camera is moved to this plot** (as the wonder tabs' (Info Screen) text does), with distinct art for normal plot, defended city, and captured city battles). Icons are **hoverable to sevopedia** (or have a camera effect). **Text color** is added for Result (Won: green; Lost: red; Retreat: yellow), effective Strength (white: 100%, green: > 66%, yellow: > 33%; red <= 33%), and captured units (we gained a unit amount: green; we lost a unit amout: red). Implemented a **legend link**, and **LOG Button** (as the Timeline tab). Examples of LOG: `163 | 760 AD | Lost | 43 | A | 6 | 6.04 |  | 7.20 | 8 | 0 | Camel Archer | Longbowman | 5 | 0 | 4 | 8.10 | 5.04 | 9.00 | 9 | 0 |  |  | TERRAIN_GRASS |  | 54 | 30`, `133 | 10 BC | Won | 64 | A | 3 | 3.30 | 1.81 | 3.30 | 2 | 0 | Trireme | Galley | 1 | 0 | 2 | 1.84 |  | 2.20 | 48 | 0 |  |  | TERRAIN_COAST |  | 32 | 10`. Main files changed: [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py), [SASBattleHistory.py](/Assets/Python/SASBattleHistory.py), [CvEventManager.py](/Assets/Python/CvEventManager.py), [BugEventManager.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/BugEventManager.py), [CvUnit.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvUnit.cpp), [CvDllPythonEvents.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDllPythonEvents.cpp), [CvDllPythonEvents.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDllPythonEvents.h), [CvEventReporter.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEventReporter.cpp), [CvEventReporter.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEventReporter.h).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5802+) Added a new **Summary tab** in the Military Advisor, showing a **synthetic view** of our Military: **Support** (detailed Cost and Supply, and Unit Cap numerical breakdown (e.g., `P x R x M    (1 x 100 x 82) / 10000 = 0 gold icon char`), Military Buildings, Military Production and XP information, and Allied Hammers for total hammer value of allies' (e.g., vassals, same team) army); **Army** (detailed numerical overview for military/civilian units, Domain repartition (Land/Sea/Air), Strongest, Costliest, Total/Avg Hammers as a power estimatation of units, Power Rank (Known) (e.g., `9/11` (in fact `44/48` if debug mode is enabled for spoilers)), Top promotions, Covert Units (Invisible, Spies, Hidden Nationality), And upgradeable units costs (Min/Avg/Max/Total)); **Deployment** (Allied/Neutral/Enemy Cities/Territory/Roaming information with Avg Defense and Best defense of our cities, defensive buildings (as of now Walls and Castles (e.g., `1 / 2`)), Wounded information (Max/Avg/Min and Full/High/Medium/Low Health (e.g, `15 (100%)`)), and Battles reusing the [SASBattleHistory.py](/Assets/Python/SASBattleHistory.py) added with the new Battles Tab (Won/Retreated/Lost (e.g., `35 (33%)`)), Good-Luck Wins and Bad-Luck Losses counts (`e.g., 11 (31%)`), Best/Worst (e.g., `6.3 vs 10.0 1300 AD (39%)`)). Also added a **legend link**.

